Z||000000||MISTER_PORKY||09-22-2001||07:41 PM||||Hi gang !<BR>  I think I've seen this topic here before, but here goes again. How much trouble involved in swapping roof panels. I'm thinking of swapping a hard top for a sun roof panel. I've had the head liner and all other interior trim out of my car before, but it's been a long time. I don't remember all the details, but I remember removing all that stuff was easy. Does the windshield need to be removed and are there any fasters behind the fenders where they overlap the corner posts.<BR>    I found a roof panel with sunroof glass and all hardware for $100.00. I haven't seen it yet, but Im sure I'll have to buy a new headliner.   <BR>    Also, is it not advisable to just get the sunroof glass panel and all hardware from a junker and just cut a hole in the hard top ? I've hard cutting the existing roof is hard to do without it splitting ! <BR>   Thanks for the help !<P>††† GOD BLESS THE U.S.A. †††||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||09-22-2001||09:14 PM||||I just removed the roof panel from my parter as I am considering the reverse swap.  I seem to have terminal leaks and it's pretty irritating.<BR>Anyway the removal was very simple. Along with the inside bolts, there are screws along the base of the windshield and the everpresent black goop.<BR>Gary||||reg||12
Z||000002||MISTER_PORKY||09-22-2001||10:23 PM||||Gary,<BR>   Don't quite understand what you meant about a reverse swap. Are you making a hard top out of a sun roof ? Actually I found an '88gt in mint condition, but it's a hard top. I really want a t-top, but might be willing to settle for a sun roof, and this gt I found is really really nice for a darn good price ! It's being a tough descision for me ! Does the windshield have to come out ? I have an '84 SE hard top that I bought brand new. It's in great shape. I want to keep it original !<BR>   Thanks for the reply !<P>     ††† GOD BLESS AMERICA †††<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||09-22-2001||10:56 PM||||No the windshield doesn't have to come out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> my 2 cents worth hehe<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/g-flag-sig.gif">  <FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||09-23-2001||10:49 AM||||Its not that hard to swap roofs. Its really one of those things that shouldn't be hard, but allmost allways gets screwed up. I did it between my 84 and 88(switched roofs). Just be VERY carefull to not crack the windshield. I was doing my best and being very carefull, but I somehow managed to break BOTH windshields of my fieros.<BR>I was NOT happy, after this happend I had a few choice words and didnt get over it for about a week. And its cost 150$ each to install windshields in both my fieros.<P>I think to install ttops is allot harder, involving frame cuting/ect.<P>Anyways good luck whatever you do!<P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000005||rogergarrison||09-23-2001||01:03 PM||||how would you take off the whole roof without taking out windshield? it mounts to top and both side pillars.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroBUZZ||09-23-2001||02:36 PM||||The windshield is bonded to the metal skeleton.  The 'glass roof panel comes off totally separate. Master S is quite right, if you try to pry the roof panel from the goop anywhere near the windshield it WILL crack.  Use a piece of wood from the out side and gently let the pressure release the bond.<BR>If you have a complete sunroof car you should have all the parts and trim you need.<P>I have a panel off in the yard if anyone needs a pic let me know.  You can see where the bolts and glue joints are. <BR>Gary ||||reg||14
